# Everyday talk (doc 30) by place and by region: the tavern, the chapel, the gate, the shore, the barracks, the
# hall, the market; and small talk with a town's own colour. Alternatives are written in parallel.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Places

scene ev_pl_tavern_fire
when topic=smalltalk place=tavern
a : Shove over, let me near the fire. | This ale tastes of the barrel. | Who's paying for this round?
b[innkeeper] : Complaints go out the door. Coin goes on the counter.
b : There's room by the dog. | All ale tastes of barrel. | Not me. I paid last time.
a : The dog can shove over too. | Not like this. This is the barrel itself. | You never paid in your life.

scene ev_pl_tavern_late
when topic=smalltalk place=tavern time=night
a : One more and I'm going home. | I said one more an hour ago. | Is the landlord watering this?
b[innkeeper] : The landlord can hear you. And no.
b : You said that an hour ago. | And here we are. | Tastes like it.
a : I meant it then too. | Here we are indeed. | Tastes like puddle.

scene ev_pl_chapel_quiet
when topic=smalltalk place=chapel
a : It's peaceful in here. | The candles smell of honey. | I haven't been inside since I was a pup.
b[priest] : The doors are always open. Come more often.
b : Peaceful, and cold. | Beeswax. The good kind. | It hasn't changed.
a : Cold's good for the soul, they say. | Someone pays well for them. | Neither have I, much.

scene ev_pl_chapel_sermon
when topic=smalltalk place=chapel|street day=rest
a : Long sermon this morning. | Did you understand the sermon? | The priest was in a mood today.
b[priest] : I heard that. The Bright One heard it too.
b : My tail went numb. | Something about order and duty. | Somebody must've sinned.
a : Mine fell asleep entirely. | It's always that. | Not me. This week.

scene ev_pl_gate_queue
when topic=smalltalk place=gate
a : The gate line's longer every day. | Why do they search every cart? | Half the country's coming through here.
b[guard] : Because last week someone hid a stolen calf under the turnips.
b[carter] : Two hours I waited. Two hours!
b : Market day, maybe. | Orders. Always orders. | And leaving by noon.
a : Every day's market day now. | Somebody's orders. | Where are they all going?

scene ev_pl_gate_strangers
when topic=smalltalk place=gate
a : Strange scents on the road today. | Those travellers didn't smell like anywhere I know. | Lot of foreign tongues at the gate.
b[guard] : We note everyone who passes. Don't you worry.
b : From the far roads, maybe. | Southern, maybe. Spicy. | Trade's good.
a : Far roads. | Spice and dust. | Trade's good for someone.

scene ev_pl_shore
when topic=smalltalk place=shore
a : Water's cold enough to stop your heart. | Tide's out farther than I've ever seen. | Found a shell big as my paw.
b[fisher] : Low tide means a storm coming. Mark it.
b[sailor] : Seen bigger. Out past the Isle, they're big as shields.
b : Don't swim, then. | Strange. | Keep it. Luck.
a : Wasn't planning on it. | It makes me uneasy. | I'll keep it on my sill.

scene ev_pl_barracks
when topic=smalltalk place=barracks
a : These cots were made for pups. | Who stole my good blanket? | Sergeant's in a foul temper.
b[soldier] : Complain to the quartermaster. He'll laugh at you.
b : Sleep on the floor, then. | Not me. | When isn't he?
a : The floor's warmer. | Somebody did. | Fair point.

scene ev_pl_hall
when topic=smalltalk place=hall
a : The council's sitting late again. | Look at the carvings on these beams. | It's always cold in the hall.
b[official] : Matters of state take time. As do petitions. As do you.
b : They love the sound of their voices. | Old work. Very old. | Big rooms always are.
a : More than we do. | Older than the town, they say. | And small purses.

scene ev_pl_market_haggle
when topic=smalltalk place=market
a : That cloth seller wanted a fortune. | I haggled her down by half! | Everything's a penny more than last market.
b[merchant] : And she'll still feed her pups. Haggling's a dance, not a war.
b : Walk away. They always call you back. | Teach me how. | Always is.
a : She didn't call me back. | Look sad. Very sad. | Always is.

scene ev_pl_market_crowd
when topic=smalltalk place=market day=market
a : I can't move for elbows today. | Mind your purse in this crush. | Everyone in the country's come to market.
b[guard] : Keep your coin in your fur, not your belt.
b : Market day. | Always do. | And their cousins.
a : I'll come early next time. | I'll keep a paw on it. | Their cousins' cousins.

scene ev_pl_home_chores
when topic=smalltalk place=home
a : The roof needs patching before the rain. | I swept and there's still sand in every corner. | Whose turn is it to fetch water?
b[spouses] : Yours. It's always yours. You know that.
b[child] : Not mine! I did it yesterday!
b : I'll help Restday. | It follows us in on our paws. | Yours.
a : You said that last Restday. | Sand and fur, everywhere. | I knew it.

scene ev_pl_field_long
when topic=smalltalk place=field
a : These rows go on forever. | Look how high the barley's grown. | Rest a moment under the oak?
b[farmer] : Rest's for winter. Bend your back.
b : Halfway now. | Good year coming. | Just a moment.
a : Halfway to forever. | Pray it holds. | Just one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Regions: the north and the coast

scene ev_rg_ridgemere_rain_forever
when topic=smalltalk region=ridgemere
a : Has it stopped raining once this year? | I think I'm growing moss. | My shutters are swollen shut again.
b[old] : It stopped once. The summer I was nine. A Restday, I think.
b[child] : I like the rain. The gutters are rivers.
b : Not that I've seen. | Green suits you. | Kick them.
a : I don't believe it ever stops. | Mossy and miserable. | I kicked. Now my toe hurts.

scene ev_rg_ridgemere_sump
when topic=smalltalk region=ridgemere place=street|tavern|market
a : Don't take the Sump stairs after dark. | Someone lost a purse down in the Sump again. | The Sump smells worse than ever.
b[guard] : We patrol the Sump in fours now. Ask yourself why.
b : I never do. | Of course they did. | Something died, maybe.
a : Wise. | Never to be seen again. | Something always has.

scene ev_rg_ridgemere_houses
when topic=smalltalk region=ridgemere
a : Brinewater's wolves were strutting about the quay. | Did you see House Vesk's banner on the new smokehouse? | The House wolves think the rain falls only on us.
b[noble] : The Houses keep this city alive. Mind your tongue.
b : Strutting like gulls. | Fish and salt, everywhere. | It does fall only on us. Have you seen their roofs?
a : Gulls with purses. | Vesk wants every shed in Ridgemere. | Slate. Fine slate.

scene ev_rg_saltreach_tide
when topic=smalltalk region=saltreach
a : Spring tide tonight. | Salt in my fur, salt in my bread, salt in my dreams. | The gulls are thick on the pans.
b[fisher] : Bring the boats high. Spring tides take what's left low.
b : Watch the pan walls. | That's Saltreach. | Something's dead out there.
a : I'll check them before dark. | All of it. | Always is.

scene ev_rg_accord_scholars
when topic=smalltalk region=accord
a : The archive scholars came through with their carts again. | A warden walked past me today. My fur stood on end. | Everyone in Upper Accord walks like they're late for prayers.
b[scholar] : Manuscripts must be moved with care. We aren't sightseeing.
b[guard] : Wardens go where they please. Best not stare.
b : What do they want out here? | They have that effect. | They usually are.
a : Old books, always. | I didn't stare. Much. | Slower, then. Pray slower.

scene ev_rg_accord_quickened
when topic=smalltalk region=accord
a : Do you think the wardens really train Quickened here? | They brought another one in, they say. Guarded on all sides. | I'd hate to be Quickened. All eyes on you.
b[priest] : Every gift is the Bright One's, and every gift needs order.
b : So they say. | Poor thing. | Better that than ordinary.
a : So they say. | Poor thing, or dangerous thing. | Maybe. I'm not so sure.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Regions: the south and the river

scene ev_rg_serferro_white
when topic=smalltalk region=ser_ferro
a : They're plastering the walls on the river street again. | Sun off these white walls is blinding. | Have you ever seen the cathedral at noon?
b[official] : The city keeps its face clean. It's in the charter.
b[priest] : The silver on the spire was a gift from three Crowns.
b : Every spring. | Squint and bear it. | Takes your breath away.
a : Clean face, dirty purse, my father said. | Squinting all summer. | Every time.

scene ev_rg_serferro_river
when topic=smalltalk region=ser_ferro place=street|shore|market
a : River's low this year. | Barges stacked three deep at the wharves. | Smell the river? Mud and money.
b[sailor] : Low water, high prices. The barges ground at the shallows.
b[merchant] : River goods keep this city fat.
b : Long dry spell. | Busy year. | Mud and money, yes.
a : It needs rain. | Busy for someone. | Mostly mud, near the tanners.

scene ev_rg_serferro_gardens
when topic=smalltalk region=ser_ferro season=spring|summer
a : The guild gardens are in flower. | Smell the orange trees by the hall? | Some lord's fountain is running again.
b[noble] : The gardens are open to the respectable. On certain days.
b : Lovely, aren't they. | Like summer itself. | For his guests, no doubt.
a : I'd like to sit in one. | I stand there and breathe. | And never for us.

scene ev_rg_cinderbrook_soot
when topic=smalltalk region=marches
a : Soot in my water bowl again. | The furnace glow lights the whole valley at night. | Hammers ringing since before dawn.
b[smith] : That's the sound of good iron. Learn to love it.
b[miner] : At least it's warm up here.
b : You get used to it. | Pretty, in a way. | Never stops.
a : I never have. | Hard to sleep under. | Never.

scene ev_rg_amberford_grass
when topic=smalltalk region=steppe
a : Nothing but grass from here to the sky. | The wind never rests out here. | You can see a rider coming a day away.
b[herder] : Good grass, fat herds. What else does a wolf need?
b : It's peaceful. | Hold onto your hat. | Gives you time to hide.
a : Too peaceful, some days. | Lost two hats this year. | Or to put the kettle on.

scene ev_rg_fens_peat
when topic=smalltalk region=fens
a : The peat smoke gets into everything. | Mist on the fens so thick I lost the path. | Will-o'-wisps over the bog again last night.
b[old] : Don't follow the lights. My brother did.
b[healer] : The fens grow every herb a healer needs. And some she doesn't.
b : I like the smell. | Follow the reed posts. | Marsh gas, nothing more.
a : It smells like home. | I nearly walked into the water. | Marsh gas that dances?

scene ev_rg_lake_mist
when topic=smalltalk region=lake
a : Mist sitting on the lake like a blanket. | Boats out early this morning. | The lake's glass-still today.
b[fisher] : Still water, no wind, no fish. Lake sulks like a wife.
b[sailor] : The Isle's hidden in that mist. I don't like it.
b : Pretty, isn't it. | They always are. | Good day for a swim.
a : Cold, though. | Lucky fish. | Brave of you.

scene ev_rg_downs_hills
when topic=smalltalk region=downs
a : Sheep on every hill, as far as you can see. | The downs are gold in this light. | Wind smells of thyme up on the ridge.
b[herder] : And every one of them a fool. I love them.
b : Never seen so many. | Very fine. | Lovely.
a : Fools and wool. | It's a good country. | Makes me want to roll in it.

scene ev_rg_fortress_walls
when topic=smalltalk region=fortresses
a : Same walls, same faces, every day. | Wind howls through these arrow slits all night. | Rations are thinner than they were.
b[soldier] : Ask for a transfer, then. See where they send you.
b : That's soldiering. | Stuff them with rags. | Supply cart's late.
a : That's my life now. | I'd have to steal rags. | Isn't it always.

scene ev_rg_ghost_town
when topic=smalltalk region=ghost_town
a : I heard the bell in the old chapel ring. There's no rope. | Nobody comes here for good reasons. | The wind sounds like voices in these ruins.
b[old] : This was a fine town once. Before.
b : The wind, surely. | Then why are we here? | Only the wind.
a : Surely. | Same as everyone. Nowhere else. | I keep telling myself.
